{"id":"project-LICHEN-worker6-3ce2","title":"[review] project-LICHEN-worker6-69p2: Ack complete flag lost in from_bytes parsing","description":"`Ack::write_to` stores the `self.complete` flag in bit 0 of byte 1 (`((self.window & 1) << FRAGMENT_N) | (if self.complete { 1 } else { 0 })`). However, `Ack::from_bytes_for` never extracts this bit - it always calls `Ack::new(data[0], window, bitmap, false)` with `complete=false`. The complete flag cannot round-trip, and a complete ACK (C=1) is silently parsed as an incomplete ACK.

